<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Frankfurt (Oder)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1506">1506</a>–<a href="/years/1811">1811</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Viadrina, Alma Mater Viadrina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> an der Oder, called the Viadrina, was founded in 1506 by Elector Joachim I as the first university of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>. It trained generations of officials, jurists and clergy for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-prussia">Brandenburg-Prussia</a> until it was merged into the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Breslau</a> in 1811. In 1991 it was refounded as the European University Viadrina.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-frankfurt-oder.jpg" alt="University of Frankfurt (Oder)" width="320" height="307" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: upload: Poznaniak1975 (http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedysta:Poznaniak1975) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SiegelViadrina.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
